  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We Effect ALCANCE  Moz 2024-2027 - We Effect ALCANCE  Moz 2023-2027- Phase 1</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">We Effect ALCANCE  Moz 2024-2027</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ALCANCE (Programa de Alimentos, Clima, Agricultura, Natureza, Coordenac&#xe3;o e Empoderamento da Mulher) Projektets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att &#x201c;bidra till att partnerorganisationer f&#xe5;r &#xf6;kad tillg&#xe5;ng till produktiv mark, tillg&#xe5;ng till och kontroll &#xf6;ver produktionsmedel samt &#xf6;kad kunskap hos kvinnor och sm&#xe5;bruksb&#xf6;nder f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla r&#xe4;tten till n&#xe4;ringsrik mat&#x201d;. Ut&#xf6;ver detta har projektet sex &#xf6;vergripande resultatomr&#xe5;den: i) Effektivt sk&#xe4;ligt och r&#xe4;ttvist livsmedelsystem, ii) h&#xe5;llbar f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning, iii) klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringar och motst&#xe5;nd, iv) j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, v) sk&#xe4;lig och r&#xe4;ttvis tillg&#xe5;ng till l&#xe4;mpliga bost&#xe4;der och vi) starkare organisation.
ALCANCE projektet kommer, f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; det &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;let och resultatet, fokusera p&#xe5; aktiviteter i tre provinser i norra Mocambique: Nampula, Niassa och Cabo Delgado. Huvuds&#xe4;tet f&#xf6;r den &#xf6;vergripande programsamordningen f&#xf6;r projektet kommer att vara We Effects kontor i Lichinga, Niassa. Genom att rikta in sig p&#xe5; de tre nordligaste provinserna i Mocambique, &#xe4;r det Sidas bed&#xf6;mning att projektet ligger v&#xe4;l i linje med det &#xf6;kade geografiska fokus som Sveriges strategi f&#xf6;r utvecklingssamarbete har valt att fokusera p&#xe5;.
Sedan 1991 har We Effect implementerat flertalet program i samband med det svenska utvecklingssamarbetet i Mocambique, med ett f&#xf6;rsta f&#xe4;ltkontor i den norra provinsen Niassa som genomf&#xf6;rde insatser s&#xe5; som Programa de Apoio a Sociedade Civil -PASC (contribution ID 23000249) och Agricultura e Recursos Naturais - ARENA (contribution ID 51140056). Det st&#xf6;rsta bilaterala samarbetet med den svenska ambassaden var genom Actions for an Inclusive and Accountable Governance (AGIR II), ett projekt som p&#xe5;gick mellan 2010&#x2013;2020 och som hade f&#xf6;ljande delprogram: Natural Resources, Agriculture, Climate Change, and Environment (NACE). Vid implementering av NACE, f&#xf6;rvaltade We Effect cirka 176 miljoner svenska kronor. &#xc5;r 2020, n&#xe4;r AGIR II-programmet slutf&#xf6;rdes, kom de &#xf6;verens om en f&#xf6;rl&#xe4;ngning av NACE-delprogram, till december 2021.
ALANCE projektet f&#xf6;resl&#xe5;s implementeras i tv&#xe5; etapper. Budgeten f&#xf6;r den f&#xf6;rsta fasen som &#xe4;r p&#xe5; tv&#xe5; &#xe5;r uppg&#xe5;r till totalt 75,8 MSEK / 456,44 MMZN (1 SEK = 6,017 MZN) och presenteras p&#xe5; kostnadsbasis med sex huvudsakliga rubriker: 66,7 % f&#xf6;r fond&#xf6;verf&#xf6;ringar till partners vilket motsvarar 50,6 MSEK (312,2 MMZN) och 33,3 % motsvarande 25,2 MMSEK (144,2 MMZN) f&#xf6;r We Effect ledda aktiviteter, &#xf6;vervakning och utv&#xe4;rdering, programpersonalskostnader, programst&#xf6;dskostnader samt administrationskostnader. Ambassaden bed&#xf6;mer att budgeten &#xe4;r rimlig i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till m&#xe5;len och att den f&#xf6;rser underlag f&#xf6;r ett kostnadseffektivt genomf&#xf6;rande av projektet.
D&#xe5; samarbetspartnern kommer inkludera vidarebefordran av medel till tredje part (forwarding of funds) genom olika finansieringsformer, &#xe4;ven om We Effect har system f&#xf6;r planering, uppf&#xf6;ljning, rapportering, utv&#xe4;rdering och l&#xe4;rande p&#xe5; plats, &#xe4;r det ambassadens analys att b&#xe5;de den &#xe5;terkommande ekonomiska uppf&#xf6;ljningen och den operativa uppf&#xf6;ljningen av samarbetspartnerna beh&#xf6;ver st&#xe4;rkas f&#xf6;r att s&#xe4;kerst&#xe4;lla att Sida-medel anv&#xe4;nds p&#xe5; r&#xe4;tt s&#xe4;tt f&#xf6;r att uppn&#xe5; f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntade projektresultat.
Sammanfattningsvis bed&#xf6;mer Sida att effekten av ALCANCE bidraget l&#xe4;gger grunden f&#xf6;r ett effektivt och r&#xe4;ttvist system, h&#xe5;llbar f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning, f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet och motst&#xe5;ndskraftiga samh&#xe4;llen i f&#xf6;rh&#xe5;llande till klimatf&#xf6;r&#xe4;ndringarna. Detta genom att partnerorganisationerna ges m&#xf6;jlighet att &#xf6;ka sin tillg&#xe5;ng till produktiv mark, tillg&#xe5;ng och b&#xe4;ttre kontroll &#xf6;ver produktionsmedlem samt &#xf6;ka kunskapen hos kvinnor och sm&#xe5;bruksb&#xf6;nder om r&#xe4;tten till mat i de tre provinserna som projektet riktar sig till, Niassa, Nampula och Cabo Delgado.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the ALCANCE (Programa de Alimentos, Clima, Agricultura, Natureza, Coordenac&#xe3;o e Empoderamento da Mulher) Contribution is &quot;Empowered partner organisations for increased access to productive land, access, and control of means of production, and increased knowledge by women and stallholder farmers to ensure the right of nutritious food&quot; and, has six overarching results areas (RA) namely: i) Effective equitable and just food systems, ii) Sustainable livelihoods, iii) Climate change and resilience, iv) Gender equality, v) Equitable and just access to adequate housing and vi) Stronger organization. 
To achieve the overall goal and results, the ALCANCE programme will focus its activities in three provinces located in the northern part of Mozambique namely: Nampula, Niassa and Cabo Delgado. We Effect will use its Lichinga Office in Niassa, as the main hub for the overall programme coordination. Sida assesses that the target provinces are well aligned with the increased geographic focus of the Swedish operationalisation plan. 
We Effect has been implementing several programmes related to Swedish Development cooperation in Mozambique since 1991, with its first field office in the northern province of Niassa on which implemented interventions such as the Programa de Apoio a Sociedade Civil -PASC (contribution ID 23000249) and the Agricultura e Recursos Naturais - ARENA (contribution ID 51140056).  The major bilateral partnership with the Swedish Embassy was through the Actions for an Inclusive and Accountable Governance (AGIR II) programme, 2010-2020 with its sub-programme entitled Natural Resources, Agriculture, Climate Change, and Environment (NACE). For the implementation of NACE, We Effect managed approximately 176 million Swedish Krona. In 2020 as AGIR II programme was being finalized, however an extension of the NACE sub-programme until December 2021 was agreed.
The ALCANCE programme is proposed to be implemented in two phases. The  budget for the first phase of  two years amounts to a total amount of 75, 8 MSEK / 456, 44 MMZN (1 SEK = 6,017 MZN),  is presented on a cost-basis with 6 main headers: 66,7% for Funds transfers to partners equal to 50,6 MSEK (312,2 MMZN) and  33,3% equal to 25,2 MMSEK (144,2 MMZN) for We Effect lead activities,  Monitoring and evaluation, Programme staff costs, Programme support costs and Administration overhead. The Embassy assesses that the budget is reasonable in relation to the objectives and provides for a basis for a cost-efficient implementation of the programme.
Since the cooperation partner will have a component of forwarding of funds to third parties&#x2019; trough different funding modalities, even though We Effect has systems for planning, monitoring, reporting, evaluation and learning in place, the Embassy&apos;s analysis is that both the recurring financial monitoring and operational monitoring of the partners need to be strengthened to ensure that Sida funding is applied properly to achieve the expected programme results.
In conclusion,  Sida assesses that the impact of the ALCANCE contribution, lay the ground for an effective, equitable and systems, sustainable livelihoods, improved gender equality and resilient communities to climate change through empowering partner organizations to increase their access to productive land, access and better control of the means of productions as well as increasing the knowledge by women and smallholders farmers about the right to food of three target provinces, Niassa, Nampula and Cabo Delgado.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall aim of the ALCANCE program is &quot;Empowered partner organisations for increased access to productive land, access, and control of means of production, and increased knowledge by women and smallholder farmers to ensure the right of nutritious food&quot;. 

The programme has six overarching results areas: 

RA1: Effective equitable and just food systems

RA2: Sustainable livelihoods.

RA3: Climate change and resilience

RA4: Gender equality

RA5: Equitable and just access to adequate housing

RA6: Stronger organisations

Alcance focus its activities in the three northern provinces (Nampula, Niassa and Cabo Delgado), and is implemented jointly with 10 implementing organizations/partners. The theory of change is based on the value of strengthening these local organisations to be effective and sustainable both as organisations and in their relevant role to deliver results as the key drivers and influencers of the change toward a rights-based society. We Effect and partners are working towards the above mentioned six results areas, to achieve fundamental structural changes at individual, household, community, organisational, policy and state levels, to empower smallholder farmer, especially women, youth and other marginalized groups to access/have the right to just and adequate, sustainable and nutritious food.</narrative>
  </description>
